Three types of Treasures Chests appear in {{EoW}}. The first is a regular variety found throughout [[Hyrule]], the second is a locked variety found in [[Monster Outpost]]s, and the third is a large variety in [[Dungeon]]s that contain [[Big Key]]s. Regular Treasure Chests are able to be manipulated using [[Bind]]. If there is an [[Object]] placed on top of a Treasure Chest, [[Princess Zelda]] is unable to open them.

==Origins==
The presence of myriad Treasure Chests throughout the worlds of the ''Zelda'' universe is a mostly unexplained phenomenon. According to the {{ALttP|-}} official Nintendo Player's Guide, Treasure Chests, hand-crafted by skilled artisans, were used by the Hyrulean people to safeguard their family heirlooms and other treasures.<ref>{{Cite Guide|ALttP Nintendo|quote= Many Hyrulian people saved family heirlooms and other treasures in Chests handcrafted by skilled artisans. Historians found them in Hyrulian homes and mountain caves. Inside they discovered jewels, armor, and arrows.|page= 30}}</ref>

==Varieties==
===Small Chests===
{| style="text-align: center;" align=right
| [[File:LADX Treasure Chest Sprite.png]]
