{{Noncanon|End}}

==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
Treasure Chests are hidden around the [[Scenarios]], either in odd corners of the map or in plain sight. Some are even partially buried, requiring the use of [[Magnesis]] to unearth them. They can contain [[Weapons]], 100-300 Rupees, or uncommon to rare [[Material]]s for [[Side Quest#Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity|Quest]] completion.
{{Noncanon|End}}

==={{CoH|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
Treasure Chests appear in {{CoH}}. They can be destroyed to reveal their contents.
{{Noncanon|End}}

==Trivia==
*Artwork of Link from {{TLoZ|-}} opening a Treasure Chest exists, despite Treasure Chests not appearing in that game.
{{Not Trivia}}
*Starting in {{OoT}} and later non-top-down 3D {{TLoZ|-}} games, Link will kick small Treasure Chests open rather than lifting the lid up with his hands. In {{BotW}} and {{TotK}}, he will stub his toe while opening a Treasure Chest without any Armor covering his legs. For [[Sheikah]]- or [[Zonai]]-style Treasure Chests, this will only happen if they are interacted with from the side and back, or if they are not upright, as Link will use his [[Sheikah Slate]] or his [[Right Arm]] to open it instead. Similarly, if Link is crouching and opens a non-Sheikah- or Zonai-style Treasure Chest, he will punch them open. If he is not wearing any torso Armor, he will react to the pain of hitting a hard object with his hands.
*In {{TP|-}}, if Link opens a Chest containing Rupees with a value of 20 or more inside and does not have sufficient room in his [[Wallet]], the Rupees are put back in the Chest and can be retrieved at a later time.<ref>{{Cite|You got a red Rupee (20)! But it won't fit in your wallet now, so let's put it back.|N/A|TP}}</ref> In every other game, including {{TPHD|-}}, the surplus Rupees are lost.
*There is a Treasure Chest in the Temple of the Ocean King in {{PH|-}} that contains nothing at all. The chest contained a Key which was taken by Linebeck before Link and Ciela arrived.<ref>{{Cite|Oh, no! It's empty... I wonder if someone got it before us...|Ciela|PH}}</ref>
*The unactivated, "invisible" Treasure Chests in the [[Earth Temple]] of {{TWW}} utilize an advanced image distortion effect with a few glitches, such as reflection of any object in front of the Chest. The distorted image has a lower resolution than the main game, probably to save processing power.

